                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1117280-951f-3d30-9db9-19381e47e0db",
                                        "entry_id": "ef575b10-749a-37eb-ab1a-f40a35e5d926",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having meaning, significant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a00ed4c4-9c51-4571-8d61-f623a8100da4",
                                                "sense_id": "f1117280-951f-3d30-9db9-19381e47e0db",
                                                "text": "I think we made a meaningful contribution to this project today."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc75034a-1d58-4b18-8104-224d48625ab8",
                                                "sense_id": "f1117280-951f-3d30-9db9-19381e47e0db",
                                                "text": "\"This baby is the one that counts. I dare say Polly here wouldn't want any other, would you, Polly?\"\n\"This baby, this baby,\" said Polly.\nWolcott gave Peter Horn a meaningful look. Horn interpreted it correctly. This baby or no more Polly ever again. This baby or Polly would be in a quiet room somewhere staring into space for the rest of her life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7738e850-13a1-43a7-ad79-427fb2aa468d",
                                                "sense_id": "f1117280-951f-3d30-9db9-19381e47e0db",
                                                "text": "But the Danes remained resolute in defence - largely thanks to a spirited display by captain Daniel Agger - and they went ahead with their first meaningful attack."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "431d38b8-273a-442f-aa16-5357e60113cc",
                                                "sense_id": "f1117280-951f-3d30-9db9-19381e47e0db",
                                                "text": "In setting out a broad-brush approach, the Arriva-owned operator doesn't make any specific requirements, but it says the replacement trains \"must achieve a meaningful reduction in the exhaust emissions and exterior noise levels compared to Chiltern's existing DMUs\"."
